  "findings": [
    "A printed page is where routing pays: `--limit 50 ls --format detail` takes 11.6 ms routed against 1,162 ms direct at 100K",
    "Listings of every match are no faster routed: the daemon returned full note records that the paths and count printers do not read (33,334 records for `ls --where type = task`: 745 ms routed, 737 ms direct). Routed listings printed as paths or counts now return only paths"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Measured right after a release build; load was elevated, which slows both routes",
    "Equivalence compares one run's stdout per case, not every sample",
    "Host power, frequency, background load, and OS page cache are uncontrolled"
  ]
